opensim-engine on Debian
========================

The system layout
-----------------

Installing the package makes the account the instances run as (opensim), the folders of the layout, owned by it
through dpkg-statoverride (an administrator's own override is kept), and /etc/opensim/opensim.conf, left as it is
once written:

  /etc/opensim          config: opensim.conf, the grids (grids/<grid>), the enabled instances (robust.d, opensim.d)
  /var/lib/opensim      data, and the home of the account
  /var/log/opensim      logs
  /var/cache/opensim    cache
  /var/backups/opensim  backups

Each OpenSimulator release installed in /usr/share/opensim gets an install profile in opensim.conf, added and
removed with it; the latest one is the default.

The files of a grid
-------------------

Every ini file of a grid may hold a password: it is readable by its owner and the group of the web server only
(mode 640, group www-data when the machine has one), as the helpers read the settings of the grid. Each install or
upgrade of the package gives them these modes again, and adds the files a grid is missing (MoneyServer.ini).

Purge
-----

Purging the package removes /var/cache/opensim and the owner it gave to the folders of the layout. Config, data,
logs, backups and the account are kept.
